   "line": [
    "Ng4"
   ],
   "spoken": "White plays a knight to g4 — and we have a tactic. A keen tactical eye and well-developed pattern recognition are what let you finish efficiently.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 23,
   "t": 2494,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/5ppp/p3p3/1p1pn3/3N1P2/2P5/PPB3PP/RNB2RK1 b kq - 0 12",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "The c3 pawn is White's biggest target, and whenever White pushes the f-pawn with the king on g1, tactics on the a7-g1 diagonal should light up your pattern recognition. Put them together: a knight capture on c3 deflects the bishop off the diagonal. If White recaptures with the rook, we take, he takes, and we fork — the bishop can't return to d4, that square is no longer protected; had White taken with the bishop, we have other moves like d4. Then a bishop to h7, and the classic right-triangle queen rotation wins.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 5,
   "t": 2553.5,
   "fen": "rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/8/8/3pP3/2P5/PP3PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 3",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
