   "line": [
    "Nc2+"
   ],
   "spoken": "One funny moment: after a knight to c2, a king to d1...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 19,
   "t": 2637,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pp2pppp/2n5/3P1b2/8/1QN2N2/PPn2PPP/R1BK1B1R b kq - 2 10",
   "line": [
    "Kd1"
   ],
   "spoken": "...if the king went to e2 there'd be a fork. Black's best move is hilarious and you have to know it.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 21,
   "t": 2647.5,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pQ2pppp/2n5/3P1b2/8/2N2N2/PP3PPP/n1BK1B1R b kq - 0 11",
   "line": [
    "Nxa1",
    "Qxb7"
   ],
   "spoken": "Because a knight capture on a1 gets dangerous after a queen to b7 — the only cleanly winning move is a6, pure prophylaxis: it prepares a knight to a5 trapping the queen and kills White's bishop-b5 ideas.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 14,
   "t": 2680,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pp2pppp/2n5/3n1b2/3P4/2N2N2/PP3PPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 4 8",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "White gets a tempo to move the rook, but the knight drops back with the threat of a bishop to c2 and b1, and you win.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 15,
   "t": 2687,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pp2pppp/2n5/3n1b2/2BP4/2N2N2/PP3PPP/R1BQK2R b KQkq - 5 8",
   "line": [
    "Bc4"
   ],
   "spoken": "The queen to b3 isn't most popular online — I face a bishop to c4 most.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 16,
   "t": 2688.5,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pp3ppp/2n1p3/3n1b2/2BP4/2N2N2/PP3PPP/R1BQK2R w KQkq - 0 9",
   "line": [
    "e6"
   ],
   "spoken": "And then just e6 with a fantastic position.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 8,
   "t": 2692,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/5n2/3P4/3p4/2P5/PP3PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 1 5",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 9,
   "t": 2693,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/5n2/3P4/3Q4/2P5/PP3PPP/RNB1KBNR b KQkq - 0 5",
   "line": [
    "Qxd4"
   ],
   "spoken": "If White plays a queen recapture on d4, that's not dangerous either.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 10,
   "t": 2699,
   "fen": "rnb1kb1r/pp2pppp/5n2/3q4/3Q4/2P5/PP3PPP/RNB1KBNR w KQkq - 0 6",
   "line": [
    "Qxd5"
   ],
   "spoken": "You can play a queen recapture on d5, or a knight recapture...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 12,
   "t": 2702.5,
   "fen": "rnb1kb1r/pp2pppp/8/3n4/8/2P5/PP3PPP/RNB1KBNR w KQkq - 0 7",
   "line": [
    "Qxd5",
    "Nxd5"
   ],
   "spoken": "...and Black has a pleasant endgame.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 7,
   "t": 2704.5,
   "fen": "rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/8/3P4/3p4/2P5/PP3PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 4",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 8,
   "t": 2705.5,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/5n2/3P4/3p4/2P5/PP3PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 1 5",
   "line": [
    "Nf6"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 9,
   "t": 2707,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/5n2/3P4/2Pp4/8/PP3PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 5",
   "line": [
    "c4"
   ],
   "spoken": "Some people play c4 here, thinking they're clever defending the pawn.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 10,
   "t": 2713.5,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pp3ppp/5n2/3Pp3/2Pp4/8/PP3PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq e6 0 6",
   "line": [
    "e5"
   ],
   "spoken": "c4 is terrible, because you play e5, and if White captures en passant you get a massive development lead.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 11,
   "t": 2717,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pp3ppp/4Pn2/8/2Pp4/8/PP3PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 6",
   "line": [
    "dxe6"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 12,
   "t": 2719.5,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pp4pp/4pn2/8/2Pp4/8/PP3PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 7",
   "line": [
    "fxe6"
   ],
   "spoken": "Actually the best recapture is with the f-pawn — and what's Black's idea?",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 13,
   "t": 2722.5,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pp4pp/4pn2/8/2Pp4/5N2/PP3PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 1 7",
   "line": [
    "Nf3"
   ],
   "spoken": "After a knight to f3, how does the f-pawn recapture make sense?",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 14,
   "t": 2733.5,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pp4pp/5n2/4p3/2Pp4/5N2/PP3PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 0 8",
   "line": [
    "e5"
   ],
   "spoken": "Very important — e5, using tactics in your favor and steamrolling the center.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 16,
   "t": 2739,
   "fen": "rnb1kb1r/pp4pp/5n2/q3N3/2Pp4/8/PP3PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 1 9",
   "line": [
    "Nxe5",
    "Qa5+"
   ],
   "spoken": "Everybody should know this idea. White's best move is elsewhere.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 7,
   "t": 2741.5,
   "fen": "rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/8/3P4/3p4/2P5/PP3PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 4",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 8,
   "t": 2742.5,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/5n2/3P4/3p4/2P5/PP3PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 1 5",
   "line": [
    "Nf6"
   ],
   "spoken": "White's best is a bishop check on b5.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 9,
   "t": 2744,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/5n2/1B1P4/3p4/2P5/PP3PPP/RNBQK1NR b KQkq - 2 5",
   "line": [
    "Bb5+"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 10,
   "t": 2745.5,
   "fen": "rn1qkb1r/pp1bpppp/5n2/1B1P4/3p4/2P5/PP3PPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 3 6",
   "line": [
    "Bd7"
   ],
   "spoken": "A bishop to d7, and the bishop back to c4 — almost nobody plays this online.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 11,
   "t": 2747,
   "fen": "rn1qkb1r/pp1bpppp/5n2/3P4/2Bp4/2P5/PP3PPP/RNBQK1NR b KQkq - 4 6",
   "line": [
    "Bc4"
   ],
   "spoken": "Here White is slightly better if he knows fifteen moves of theory.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 12,
   "t": 2757.5,
   "fen": "rn1qkb1r/p2bpppp/5n2/1p1P4/2Bp4/2P5/PP3PPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 0 7",
   "line": [
    "b5"
   ],
   "spoken": "You play b5...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 13,
   "t": 2758.5,
   "fen": "rn1qkb1r/p2bpppp/5n2/1p1P4/3p4/1BP5/PP3PPP/RNBQK1NR b KQkq - 1 7",
   "line": [
    "Bb3"
   ],
   "spoken": "...a bishop to b3, you capture and a knight recaptures on c3 — check my Title Tuesday game.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 15,
   "t": 2763,
   "fen": "rn1qkb1r/p2bpppp/5n2/1p1P4/8/1BN5/PP3PPP/R1BQK1NR b KQkq - 0 8",
   "line": [
    "dxc3",
    "Nxc3"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 16,
   "t": 2768.5,
   "fen": "rn1qkb1r/3bpppp/5n2/pp1P4/8/1BN5/PP3PPP/R1BQK1NR w KQkq - 0 9",
   "line": [
    "a5"
   ],
   "spoken": "And then a5, pushing the bishop off b3 — White can easily be worse; you fianchetto, and I like Black's practical position.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 7,
   "t": 2788,
   "fen": "rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/8/3P4/3p4/2P5/PP3PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 4",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "It's dynamic — you're playing the Smith-Morra, but on Black's terms.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 6,
   "t": 2789.5,
   "fen": "rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/8/3p4/3pP3/2P5/PP3PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 4",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 7,
   "t": 2792.5,
   "fen": "rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/8/3p4/3QP3/2P5/PP3PPP/RNB1KBNR b KQkq - 0 4",
   "line": [
    "Qxd4"
   ],
   "spoken": "In our game White grabbed with the queen, we played a knight to f6...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 8,
   "t": 2799,
   "fen": "rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/8/8/3Qp3/2P5/PP3PPP/RNB1KBNR w KQkq - 0 5",
   "line": [
    "dxe4"
   ],
   "spoken": "...though the best move was actually the capture on e4 — I should have just taken the pawn, into an endgame a clean pawn up.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 10,
   "t": 2803.5,
   "fen": "rnbk1bnr/pp2pppp/8/8/4p3/2P5/PP3PPP/RNB1KBNR w KQ - 0 6",
   "line": [
    "Qxd8+",
    "Kxd8"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 8,
   "t": 2805.5,
   "fen": "rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/8/8/3Qp3/2P5/PP3PPP/RNB1KBNR w KQkq - 0 5",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "And if White plays a queen to e4, the queen gets tossed around.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 10,
   "t": 2807,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/5n2/8/4Q3/2P5/PP3PPP/RNB1KBNR w KQkq - 1 6",
   "line": [
    "Qxe4",
    "Nf6"
   ],
   "spoken": "A knight to f6 was a little edgier and gave White more of a choice.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 8,
   "t": 2810,
   "fen": "rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/8/8/3Qp3/2P5/PP3PPP/RNB1KBNR w KQkq - 0 5",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "So after the knight to d7, instead of blundering the queen White should have taken the pawn. I planned e6 thinking we'd recover it, but I forgot about a queen to e4 — a snafu. After something like a queen to b6 we're just playing the Smith-Morra as Black: down a pawn, but great development and not easy for White. Our opponent simply didn't assume the pin was permanent.",
   "reanchor": true
  }
 ]
}